# Keep the build context small AND prevent dev/test/secret artefacts from
# being baked into the image. Anything excluded here is invisible to the
# `COPY` instructions in the Dockerfile.
#
# Matching rule to remember: .dockerignore patterns are anchored at the
# context root. `*.md` matches only top-level files; `**/x` matches at any
# depth. The last matching line wins, so re-includes (`!`) follow the
# exclusion they undo.

# --- Python build/runtime detritus (any depth) -----------------------------
# `**/` because a local `docker compose build` otherwise copies stale
# __pycache__ from a developer's tree into /app; the image compiles its own.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/*.pyd
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.hypothesis/
.import_linter_cache/
.tox/
.nox/
.cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml

# --- Local virtualenvs (must NEVER be copied — wrong arch & polluted) ------
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# --- Test code & fixtures (not part of the runtime image) ------------------
tests/
evals/
unit-test-prompt/

# --- Build-time/CI tooling (not part of the runtime image) -----------------
# tools/ci/* is the CI gate + evidence pipeline, run by GitHub Actions and
# tests/, never by the service. It also imports defusedxml, which is a dev-only
# pin and therefore absent from the production venv. The Dockerfile does not
# COPY it either; this entry is the defence-in-depth half, matching tests/ and
# skills/ above. It used to live at agents/ci/ and so WAS baked into the image
# by `COPY agents/`.
tools/

# --- Local run data and databases (never image content) --------------------
# runs/ is the local RUNS_ROOT (per-user agent sandboxes); in production
# /app/runs is a bind mount.
runs/
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.log

# --- Per-user runtime data (bind-mounted from the host at runtime) ---------
# In production /app/skills is an EBS volume, NOT baked image content.
skills/

# --- Dev-only files the Dockerfile never copies ----------------------------
# Dependencies come from pyproject.toml + uv.lock only.
requirements*.txt
Makefile
pyrightconfig.json
init_db.py

# --- Secrets & local configuration (NEVER bake into images) ----------------
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# --- Documentation (the runtime image doesn't serve docs) ------------------
# Top-level only (see the matching rule above). Deliberately NOT `**/*.md`:
# app/ and agents/ carry Markdown the runtime reads (prompts, AGENT.md,
# guardrails), and changing this would change what the image contains.
*.md
README*
# ...EXCEPT agents/ AGENT.md + guardrail .md — these are runtime DATA the agent
# loader reads from disk (not docs). Re-include so `COPY agents/` keeps them.
!agents/**/*.md
# ...and the built-in global Skills catalog. Unlike the rest of skills/ it IS
# image content: backend/Dockerfile bakes it to /app/builtin-skills/global,
# outside the /app/skills EBS mount. The last matching line wins, so these must
# stay BELOW `skills/`. Nothing else under skills/ is re-included (no per-user
# dirs, no skills/*.md docs).
!skills/global
!skills/global/**
# ...and the AI workflow builder's skill, shipped with app/ (its SKILL.md and
# reference .md files are runtime DATA, and the image build checks the main ones
# exist). Must stay BELOW `*.md`.
!app/agents/workflow_builder/skills/**
# ...and the AI workflow builder's versioned prompts (system_prompt.v*.md,
# transcript_summary.v1.md). The agent reads them from disk at import, and the image
# build checks that system_prompt.v2.md exists. Must stay BELOW `*.md`.
!app/agents/workflow_builder/prompts/*.md

# --- Git metadata ----------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# --- Docker artefacts (avoid recursive context bloat) ----------------------
Dockerfile*
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml
docker-compose*.yaml

# --- Editor / OS / misc paranoia ------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
.kiro/
.agents/
*.swp
**/node_modules/

# --- Re-excludes that must beat the re-includes above ----------------------
# A re-include such as `!skills/global/**` would otherwise bring back caches
# that live inside it.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc

# --- Secrets anywhere in the context (MUST stay last) ----------------------
# The patterns under "Secrets & local configuration" match only at the context
# root. Every directory the Dockerfile copies whole (skills/global, hooks/global,
# pptx) must still never carry one, and the last matching line wins, so this
# block is last and beats every re-include above it.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/.DS_Store
